direction: down
"derived-credit": "derived-credit\nClose acquisition directory, drain read leases,\nacquire exact Done receipt, retire root\nregistration, then release session after last\nrestoration debt"
"execution-owner": "execution-owner\nReserve no-GC stable slot and protect input under\ncaller root fence before any marker allocation;\nfailure retains caller ownership"
"root-publication": "root-publication\nPublish immutable descriptor only after VM-wide\nscanned mutable root slots are registered; nonzero\nprocessor cannot assume current RC list provides\ncoverage"
"storage-commit": "storage-commit\nVM cleanup excludes live guards, exported\ncontinuation handles and invocation leases; storage\nand old-roster duties remain parent obligations"
"marker-acquire": "marker-acquire\nReload relocated proc from registered root; publish\nfully initialized marker with one still reference\nwithout another safepoint; allocation failure owns\nno marker"
"abnormal-takeover": "abnormal-takeover\nNormal tail and admitted exceptional custodian\ncompete for same generation-aware cleanup state;\nwinner pins session and owns nonabandonable cleanup\nsegment"
"single-drop": "single-drop\nInvalidate marker then decrement exactly one owned\nstill reference; no reentry, GC, native throw or\nexecutor takeover in this segment"
"completion-receipt": "completion-receipt\nPublish Done only after cleanup and restoration\ncomplete; query lost acknowledgement using exact\nactivation and settlement identities; do not replay\nkill"
"execution-owner" -> "root-publication"
"root-publication" -> "marker-acquire"
"marker-acquire" -> "abnormal-takeover"
"abnormal-takeover" -> "single-drop"
"single-drop" -> "completion-receipt"
"completion-receipt" -> "derived-credit"
"derived-credit" -> "storage-commit"
"root-publication" -> "abnormal-takeover"
"abnormal-takeover" -> "completion-receipt"
"root-publication" -> "derived-credit"
proof: "SysML -> ASCENT -> QNT / Lean; source + platform OPEN"
"storage-commit" -> proof
gain0: "complete-marker-custody\nSafety is conditional on no-abandonment cleanup and\ncomplete exceptional landing coverage"
proof -> gain0
gain1: "registration-sharing\nShared support saves setup duplication only;\nO(A+H+I+R+T) metadata and retained unresolved roots\nremain"
proof -> gain1
gain2: "retire-duplicate-tail-policy\nOld kill sites retire only after every path routes\nthrough same marker token; no double accounting"
proof -> gain2
gain3: "modern-c-net-benefit\nPositive work balance requires actually removed\nrepeated support or setup cost to exceed added checks;\nZig-specific savings unproved"
proof -> gain3
